CREATED:20260720T183414Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260720T183414Z
UID:10001415-1787997600-1788003000@nchumanities.org
SUMMARY:Downtown Raleigh Black History Tour
DESCRIPTION:Join us to discover inspiring stories and learn more about this important part of our community’s heritage.\nThe Pope House is excited to offer walking tours showcasing Raleigh’s vibrant downtown Black history. The tour will explore parts of the Third Ward neighborhood\, Black Wall Street\, historic churches\, and more. Registration is required\, and tours will meet at the Dr. M.T. Pope House Museum. \nPlease note: The tour covers approximately 1.4 miles and lasts one hour. Rest stops are included along the route. \nDates: Every Saturday – July 11 through Sept. 12\nTime: 10 a.m.\nAges: All\nCost: $10 Adults\, $6 Children ages 6 – 17
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/downtown-raleigh-black-history-tour/2026-08-29/
LOCATION:Pope House Museum\, 511 S Wilmington St\, Raleigh\, NC\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Humanities Sector Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/pope-house-museum-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
